  "question": {
    "text": "An infinite thin non-conducting sheet has uniform surface charge density <math><mi>σ</mi></math>. Find the potential difference <math><msub><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow></msub></math> between points&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> as shown in the figure. The line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>AB</mi></math> makes an angle of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>37</mn><mo>°</mo></math> with the normal to the sheet. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mn>3</mn><mn>7</mn><mo>°</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math><br />\r<br />\r<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/denwcgcgbizynrzfbknekrzmfkiownziyebkzgqkvtciwqklic.jpeg\" />",
